    T702
        title      Adopt feature-owned module folders
        status     done
        priority   medium
        description
            Historical structural contract and Bead reconciliation: use one cohesive
            feature-owned module folder with public types, implementation, private helpers,
            codecs, and local tests. Keep entrypoints and public facades as re-exports.
            Preserve public features and semantic proof obligations.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.9 (closed). Historical writes covered
            IMPLEMENTATION_WORKFLOW.md and open implementation/validation Beads. Production
            source was not edited. Evidence: Bead lint, stale-language scan, and diff check.
        acceptance
            The implementation workflow has one module convention and no active proof-role
            folder requirement. Open Beads name an owning feature module or let the coder
            establish one; local tests use test/. Public routes remain facade-only. All
            public routes, proofs, failure lanes, and dependencies remain intact.

            Historical Bead lint, stale-language, and diff checks passed. No current result
            is implied.
        derives_from [@plan.Verification.D1, @plan.Verification.D3]

