    T716
        title      Simplify policy lint rules to broad source bans
        status     draft
        priority   high
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.26 (source status in_progress at migration); this Workflow Task remains draft.
            Replace the six named Phase 2.1 alias/data-flow analyzers with broad syntactic
            bans over packages/flow-state-rewrite/src. Each rule owns its implementation and
            focused tests; the orchestrator owns shared config and aggregate checks.

            Allowed writes: the six rule implementations and tests, plus shared lint
            configuration required to cover the whole source root. Do not edit runtime
            production code, contracts, frozen packages/flow-state, generated output, or
            refactor.md.

            Supersession: the source note cites an earlier P13 packet. Retain that citation as
            provenance; T716 is the replacement Workflow scope. Do not create duplicate Workflow
            work. This Task owns its current status.
        acceptance
            All six named rules enforce broad documented syntactic bans across the full
            rewrite source root without alias or data-flow analysis. Each has focused tests
            for broad rejection and a minimal intentional exception set; whole-source config
            is consistent.

            Aggregate anti-slop and focused rule suites, rewrite type/static checks,
            formatting, and diff checks pass. Independent architecture, contract, and bug
            reviews pass on the same final snapshot. Report remaining diagnostics accurately.
            Runtime production code remains unchanged.
        derives_from [@plan.Verification.D3, @plan.Verification.D6, @plan.Verification.V8]

    T717
        title      Remove incidental readonly from rewrite data definitions
        status     draft
        priority   medium
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-6gm (source status open at migration); prerequisite
            flow-state-591 (closed at migration).
            The closed prerequisite delivered the global rule and recorded the rewrite baseline.
            The earlier migration diff was discarded; revalidate prior findings on the current
            snapshot before claiming completion.

            Remove incidental readonly syntax and Readonly-prefixed names from ordinary
            packages/flow-state-rewrite data definitions. Preserve contract-required public,
            callback, tuple, generic, and compile-proof shapes. Keep the appropriate
            Schema.Literals([... ] as const) tuple. Treat generated declarations as build
            output and inspect changes through their owning source.
        acceptance
            Incidental readonly in ordinary rewrite data definitions is removed. Every retained
            readonly/Readonly-prefixed authored type has a concrete contract or type-proof reason
            recorded adjacent to it; the lint review signal may be locally waived with that
            reason. Required public and generic relationships remain intact and have compile-time
            proofs where applicable. Rewrite typecheck, lint, tests, build, and independent
            review pass.
